;; Regulatory source register for JPN-MOF — procurement (会計法 / 予算決算及び
;; 会計令 / 全省庁統一資格), FEFTA foreign-investment screening, and customs.
;;
;; README.md says the operator's compliance claims must rest on the official
;; MOF / Customs sources. Until this file existed there was no such list, so no
;; claim in this repository could be traced to anything. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a
;; URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it.
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be:
;;                   laws.e-gov.go.jp is a single-page app that answers
;;                   HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>, renders "not found"
;;                   client-side, and therefore cannot tell a real citation
;;                   from an invented one.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; THE HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path that
;; does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every host in the
;; register and fails if the answer has changed. A dated note saying "measured
;; to refuse correctly" degrades into a constant the moment it is written; a
;; declaration the run re-measures cannot.
;;
;; NONE OF THE THREE HOSTS CITED HERE SERVED A BOT CHALLENGE WHEN MEASURED
;; (2026-08-29). That is a measurement of one cold client on one day, not a
;; property of the hosts: www.meti.go.jp, in the sibling METI register, serves
;; an AWS WAF challenge as a 202 under repeated asking. The verifier here keeps
;; the same challenge detector, so if a challenge ever stands in for a page the
;; run REFUSES (exit 2) instead of reporting either a pass or a register error.
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-29, serial requests spaced seconds apart:
;;   www.mof.go.jp       a nonexistent path answers 404 with a real
;;                       "404 Not Found : 財務省" page at the requested URL.
;;   www.customs.go.jp   a nonexistent path answers 404 with a 196-byte body
;;                       titled "404 Not Found" at the requested URL. The FRONT
;;                       page of this host is served as Shift_JIS with no
;;                       charset in the Content-Type header -- the declaration
;;                       is in a meta tag, so a verifier reading only the
;;                       header would decode every Japanese string as mojibake
;;                       and misreport the register. :page/charset pins it.
;;   www.p-portal.go.jp  a nonexistent path answers 401 with a
;;                       "調達ポータル システムエラー" page. The front URL
;;                       redirects to the SPA entry
;;                       /pps-web-biz/UZA01/OZA0101, which is where the title
;;                       is served; the register declares that redirect
;;                       explicitly rather than citing the SPA URL as if it
;;                       were what was asked for.
;;
;; cais.go.jp (電子政府調達システム) was also probed on 2026-08-29 and could
;; not be reached at all from this client (connection failure, both the front
;; page and a nonexistent path). Nothing is cited on it, so there is no
;; :host-behaviour entity for it -- one would only make every run refuse.
;; :coverage/not-covered records it.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in a procurement / FEFTA-screening /
;; customs register. Claims stop at the level actually checked -- law identity
;; (title and law number from the e-Gov API), and for the cited pages the
;; title, the URL, the charset and the strings read on 2026-08-29. No article
;; text and no PDF is asserted, because none was read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run. A change here invalidates the check that rests
 ;; on it, which is the point of writing it down as data.

 {:source/id "host.www-mof-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.mof.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "財務省 itself. A nonexistent path answers 404 with a real
                404 Not Found : 財務省 page served AT THE REQUESTED URL, so
                the title separates a real page from this soft 404 as well as
                the status does."}

 {:source/id "host.www-customs-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.customs.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "財務省関税局 / Japan Customs. A nonexistent path answers 404
                with a 196-byte body titled 404 Not Found -- small enough to
                look like an edge error, but it is the host's own refusal.
                The front page of this host is Shift_JIS declared only in a
                meta tag; see the customs.home entry."}

 {:source/id "host.www-p-portal-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.p-portal.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 401
  :source/note "調達ポータル (the government procurement portal, run by
                財務省's procurement side). A nonexistent path answers 401 --
                not 403, not 404 -- with a 調達ポータル システムエラー page.
                A checker written to expect 404 specifically would misreport a
                host that answered perfectly clearly."}

